        <body>
            <div xml:id="d80">

                <pb facs="0180" n="84" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg84"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Pekin, China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-01-02"><hi rendition="#italic">January 2,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 304.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith
                    translation of an imperial circular and decree which have recently been sent to
                    all the viceroys, Tartar generals, and governors, but which has only just come
                    to light.</p>
                <p>It would be a hopeful indication for the future of the Empire if China either
                    could or would carry it out, which is neither probable nor possible.</p>
                <pb facs="0181" n="85" xml:id="pg85"/>
                <p>It, however, may give some encouragement to local officials, inspire them with
                    some measure of confidence in the Central Government, and by so much strengthen
                    the hands of the present unpopular dynasty.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger.</hi></signed></closer>




